
====================================================================================================
S1. The response eigenvalues at the FROZEN g_ext, both footings
====================================================================================================
  gamma_v^2_parallel = d(nu g)/dg |_g_ext        gamma_v^2_perp = nu(g_ext)
    g_ext (m/s^2)          a0  e=g_ext/a0  gamma_v par  gamma_v perp
       1.7780e-10   9.360e-11      1.8996       1.0112        1.1115
       1.7780e-10   1.130e-10      1.5735       1.0151        1.1309
       2.0780e-10   9.360e-11      2.2201       1.0086        1.0974
       2.0780e-10   1.130e-10      1.8389       1.0118        1.1147
  [OK] the PERPENDICULAR boost exceeds the parallel one (1.1115 vs 1.0112) -- the external field stiffens the response along itself, which is the EFE anisotropy
  PRIOR ART, credited: an anisotropic effective gravity in an external field is a KNOWN
  feature of MOND-type EFE treatments (Milgrom; Banik & Zhao and others have discussed it
  for wide binaries). What is new here is that it is DERIVED from this framework's action
  via Theorem B rather than prescribed, and that the frozen target turns out to be an
  orientation average of it.

====================================================================================================
S2. gamma_v(theta), the orientation average, vs the FROZEN target
====================================================================================================
  With eigenvalues (gamma^2_par, gamma^2_perp) and separation at angle theta to g_ext,
      gamma_v(theta) = [ gamma^4_par cos^2 theta + gamma^4_perp sin^2 theta ]^(1/4)
   theta (deg)   gamma_v
           0.0    1.0112
          15.0    1.0189
          30.0    1.0391
          45.0    1.0649
          60.0    1.0890
          75.0    1.1056
          90.0    1.1115
  isotropic orientation average gamma_v = 1.0799
  FROZEN MI point target = 1.09, band (1.05, 1.1)
  difference from the frozen point = -0.0101
  [OK] the DERIVED orientation-averaged gamma_v = 1.0799 lands INSIDE the frozen band (1.05, 1.1) -- the frozen target SURVIVES derivation and does not need moving
  and for comparison the frozen MG target is 1.137: the derived MI average sits
  +0.0571 from it, i.e. still inside the pre-declared 'MI-vs-MG not
  decided' zone. Amendment 2 does NOT rescue MI-vs-MG separability.

====================================================================================================
S3. The orientation SPREAD -- a sharper statistic than the frozen aggregate
====================================================================================================
  gamma_v ranges 1.0112 (separation ALONG g_ext) to 1.1115 (PERPENDICULAR)
  spread = 0.1004 in gamma_v
  frozen sigma_tot on the aggregate fit = 0.028
  spread / sigma_tot = 3.58
  [OK] the orientation spread (0.1004) is 3.6x the frozen sigma_tot -- an orientation-RESOLVED statistic is intrinsically sharper than the frozen scalar fit, and the frozen pipeline averages it away
  Both footings and both g_ext conventions:
      g_ext=primary  a0=canonical  spread = 0.1004  (3.6 sigma_tot)
      g_ext=primary  a0=alt        spread = 0.1158  (4.1 sigma_tot)
      g_ext=alt      a0=canonical  spread = 0.0888  (3.2 sigma_tot)
      g_ext=alt      a0=alt        spread = 0.1029  (3.7 sigma_tot)
  [OK] the spread exceeds sigma_tot on EVERY footing and g_ext convention (min 0.0888) -- the amendment is not footing-contingent

====================================================================================================
S4. Full NONLINEAR check at real separations (no small-h expansion)
====================================================================================================
  Solve the exact two-body relative acceleration a_1 - a_2 with the derived law, at real
  separations, and read gamma_v = sqrt(|a_rel,radial| / (GM/s^2)). M = 1 Msun total.
    s (kAU)     h/a0  gamma par  gamma perp   iso avg
        2.0   7.9215     1.0301      1.0294    1.0296
        5.0   1.2674     1.0161      1.0950    1.0783
       10.0   0.3169     1.0114      1.1102    1.0785
       20.0   0.0792     1.0112      1.1114    1.0785
       30.0   0.0352     1.0112      1.1115    1.0785
       60.0   0.0088     1.0112      1.1115    1.0785
  deep-regime (60 kAU) nonlinear result: par 1.0112, perp 1.1115, iso 1.0785
  linear-response prediction from S1/S2:  par 1.0112, perp 1.1115, iso 1.0799
  [OK] the full nonlinear solve agrees with the linear-response derivation to 0.0014 in gamma_v -- the tensor expansion is valid in the deep regime

====================================================================================================
S5. WHAT AMENDMENT 2 MUST SAY
====================================================================================================
  1. The MI-EFE law is NO LONGER A PRESCRIPTION. Theorem 5 derives it from Theorem B, so the
     frozen 'prescription flag' can be discharged -- but NOT the a0-degeneracy flag, which
     is untouched and still forbids reporting any outcome as measuring a0.
  2. THE FROZEN TARGET SURVIVES. Derived orientation-averaged gamma_v = 1.0799, inside the
     frozen band (1.05, 1.1) and 0.0101 from the point target
     1.09. No target is being moved. That is the honest and fortunate outcome: the
     amendment ADDS information without shifting a number after the fact.
  3. A NEW STATISTIC IS ADDED, and it is sharper than the frozen one. The derived EFE is
     ANISOTROPIC: gamma_v runs 1.0112 (separation along g_ext) to 1.1115
     (perpendicular), a spread of 0.1004 = 3.6x the frozen sigma_tot. The
     frozen pipeline fits ONE scalar and averages that away. Amendment 2 adds an
     ORIENTATION-RESOLVED fit: bin pairs by the angle between the projected separation vector
     and the Galactic-centre direction, and fit gamma_v per bin.
  4. THE SIGN IS PRE-DECLARED so the new statistic cannot be read post-hoc: PERPENDICULAR
     pairs must show the LARGER boost. A measured anisotropy of the opposite sense at >3
     sigma falsifies the derived EFE independently of the aggregate gamma_v.
  5. IT DOES NOT RESCUE MI-vs-MG. The derived average still sits inside the pre-declared
     'not decided' zone (+0.0571 from the MG target). Amendment 2 makes no claim there.
  6. SCOPE: equal-mass, deep-regime, projected-geometry-free. Real pairs have mass ratios and
     the observed angle is a projection, both of which DILUTE the anisotropy -- so the
     spread above is an UPPER bound on what DR4 can see, and the amendment says so.
  [OK] the amendment's content is fixed by computation, with the sign pre-declared
====================================================================================================
